{
  "abstract": "A complete Lean 4 formalization of the classical characterizations of Wolstenholme primes: for a prime p > 7, C(2p−1, p−1) ≡ 1 (mod p⁴) holds if and only if p³ divides the numerator of the harmonic number H_{p−1}, and if and only if p divides the numerator of the Bernoulli number B_{p−3}. It also proves Wolstenholme's theorem C(2p−1, p−1) ≡ 1 (mod p³) for primes p > 3, and Glaisher's congruence 3·H_{p−1,2} ≡ 2p·B_{p−3} (mod p²). The statements of the first three results are copied verbatim from Google DeepMind's Formal Conjectures. The proof of the Bernoulli characterization avoids Kummer's congruences: it combines Faulhaber's formula and von Staudt–Clausen with a doubling argument k ↦ 2k mod p.",
